He was in the desert for 40 days. There the devil tempted him. Wild animals did not harm him, Jesus. Angels watched over him. Jesus chooses the first disciples.
After John was imprisoned, Jesus went to Galilee. He preached the good news of God.
"The time has come," he said. "The Kingdom of God is near. Repent of your sins and believe the good news!"
One day Jesus was walking beside the Sea of Galilee. There he saw Simon and his brother Andrew. They were throwing a net into the lake. They were fishermen.
Come, follow me, said Jesus. "Here we will make you fishers of men."
Immediately, they emptied their nets and followed him.
After this, Jesus walked a little further. When he had done this, he saw Simon Peter's brother, Andrew, and his brother, Simon. They were in a boat, preparing their nets.
Immediately he called them. They left their father Zebdi in the boats with the hired workers. Then they followed Jesus. Jesus casts out an unclean spirit.
Jesus and those with him went to Capernaum. When the Sabbath came, he went to the synagogue. There he began to teach.
People were astonished at his teaching, for he taught them as one having authority, and not as the scribes.
In that moment, a man cried out in their assembly, and he was under the control of an evil one, so he said,
Who are you and what is this Jesus of Nazareth? Have you come to burn us? I know who you are. You are a saint of God!
"Silence!" said Jesus firmly. "Come out of him!"
The evil spirit shook the man violently. Then it came out of him with a loud cry.
Everyone was astonished. They asked one another, "What is this? A new teaching! With authority! He even commands evil spirits, and they obey him."
News about Jesus spread quickly throughout Galilee. Jesus heals many people.
Jesus and those with him went out of the synagogue. They went with James and John to the house of Simon and Andrew.
Simon's mother-in-law was lying in bed. She had a fever. They told Jesus about this.
She's fine now. Take her hand and help her up. The fever has left her. After that, she started serving them.
And it came to pass, that afterward Jesus went throughout Galilee, teaching in their synagogues, and preaching the gospel of the kingdom, and healing all manner of sickness and all manner of disease among the people. And his fame went throughout all Syria: and they brought unto him all sick people that were taken with divers diseases and torments, and those which were possessed with devils, and those which were lunatick, and paralytic; and he healed them.
All the people in the city gathered at the gate.
Jesus healed many of them. They had all kinds of diseases. And he cast out many demons. But he did not give them permission to speak, because they knew who he was. Jesus prayed in a quiet place.
It was a very early morning, and darkness still covered everything. Jesus got up and left the house. He went to a place where he could be alone there. There he prayed.
Simon and his companions went out to look for Jesus.
When they found him, they cried out, "Everyone thinks you're dead!"
Then Jesus said, "Let's go to another place. I want to go to the nearby towns. We must preach there too. That is why I came."
And so he traveled throughout Galilee, preaching in their synagogues, and casting out demons. Jesus heals a man who was afflicted with leprosy.
A man who had a skin disease came to Jesus. On his knees he asked Jesus. He said, "If you are willing to make me 'clean', you can do that."
Jesus was filled with profound anxiety. He reached out and touched the man. "I am willing to do that," he said. "Be clean."
Immediately his illness left him. He recovered.
Jesus let him go right away. He gave him a strong warning.
"Don't tell that to the guy," he said. "Go and show yourself to the priest. Make the sacrifices that Moses commanded. This is a testimony to the priest and the people that you are 'clean'."
But the man went out and began to speak immediately. He spread the news to all the people. Therefore, Jesus cannot enter a city openly. He remained outside in deserted places. But people still came to him from everywhere.
Jesus heals a man who cannot walk.
After two days, Jesus entered Capernaum again. The people heard that he had come to his own house.
The people became so numerous that there was no place left. Even outside the door there was no place. And Jesus came and spoke to them the Word.
Four of those who came were carrying a man who could not walk.
But they couldn't get him close to Jesus because of the crowd. So they got a hole in the roof above Jesus. Then they lowered the man through it onto a bed.
Jesus saw their faith. So he said to the man, "Son, your sins are forgiven."
Some teachers of the law were sitting here. They were thinking.
What does it mean when that person talks like that? They're saying something good is evil! Only God forgives sins!
Immediately, Isa knew what they were thinking. For he said to them, "Why do you reason these things in your hearts?
What's better, to tell this man 'your sins are forgiven'? Or to tell him 'get up, take your reward and leave'?
"Love you. You know that the Son of Man has authority on earth to forgive sins." Then Jesus spoke to the man who could not walk.
Say to you, he said, "Rise. Take your belongings and go to your house."
A man stood up and took his cushion. Then he walked away and everyone saw him. Everyone was amazed. They praised God and said, "We have never seen anything like this!" Jesus chose Levi.
Again Jesus returned alongside the Sea of Galilee. A large crowd came to him. He began to teach them.
He went and saw Louis Ben El-Helfay. Louis was sitting in the tax collection office. "Follow me," Jesus told him. Louis got up and followed him.
And after that, Jesus was eating a meal at the house of Levi. Many tax collectors and "sinners" were eating with him and his disciples. They were part of the large crowd of people who followed Jesus.
Some of the teachers of the law who were Pharisees were there. They saw Jesus eating with "sinners" and tax collectors. So they asked his disciples, "Why does he eat with tax collectors and 'sinners'?"
Jesus heard that. So he said to them, "The one who is well has no need of a doctor, but the one who is sick does. I did not come to call the righteous to repentance, but I came to call the sinners to repentance." Jesus was asked about fasting.
The disciples of John and of the Pharisees were fasting. The people came to Jesus. They said to him, "The disciples of John fast often and make a display of this. The disciples of the Pharisees also do the same. But your disciples are not fasting. Why is this so?"
Then Jesus answered, "How can the guests fast while they are with the bridegroom? They cannot fast as long as they are with him.
But here is the opportunity that will come when the bridegroom will be taken from them. On that day they will move without eating.
People do not sew a new fabric hat on old clothes. If they did that, the new would emerge from the old. This would further ruin the break.
Some people do not make new wine in old wineskins. If they did that, the wine would burst the wineskins. And so both the wine and the wineskins would be ruined. No, everyone should make new wine in new wineskins." Jesus is Lord of the Sabbath.
One Sabbath Jesus was walking with his disciples through the grainfields. The disciples began to break off some of the heads of grain.
The Pharisees said to Jesus, "Look! It is against the law to do this on the Sabbath. Why are your disciples doing it?"
He said, "Haven't you read what David did? He and his men were coming. They needed bread."
In the time of Abiathar the high priest, David went into the house of God and ate the holy bread. It was only for the priests to eat it. David gave some of it to his men.
Then Jesus said to them, "The Sabbath was made for man's sake, and man was not made for the Sabbath's sake.
The Son of Man is lord even of the Sabbath.
The healing is on Saturday.
Again Jesus entered the temple. There was a man there with a withered, crooked hand.
Some Pharisees were trying to find fault with Jesus. They were watching him closely. They were trying to see if he would heal the man on the Sabbath day.
Jesus spoke to the man who had no weak and folded hand. "Get up in front of everyone," he told him.
Then Jesus asked them, "What does the Law say? What must we do on the Sabbath? Is it right to do good? Or is it right to do evil? Should we save a life? Or should we destroy it?" But no one answered him.
Jesus looked at them with anger. He was very angry because their hearts were hard. Then He said to the man, "Stretch out your hand." He stretched it out, and his hand was restored well.
Then the Pharisees went out and began to plot with the Herodians against Jesus. For they said, "He is destroying our nation." The crowds were following Jesus.
Jesus went to the Sea of Galilee with his disciples. A large crowd from Galilee followed him.
People heard about everything that was happening. They were coming from Judea, Jerusalem, and Edom. They were from the territories east of the Jordan River. And they came from the area of Tyre and Sidon.
Because of the large crowd, Jesus told His disciples He needed a small boat for Me. This will keep people from crowding around him.
Jesus healed many people. So the sick person was driven forward to touch him.
Wherever the people possessed by evil spirits saw him, they fell down in front of him. The spirits cried out, "You are the Son of God!"
But Jesus commanded them not to tell who he was. Jesus appoints the twelve apostles
Jesus went up a mountain. He called certain people to come to him, and they came.
He appointed 12 of them and named them apostles. From then on, they would be with him. He would also send them out to preach.
They will have the authority to expel the devil.
In Jesus' eyes, the twelve were. Simon was one of them. Jesus gave him the name Peter.
James the son of Zebedee and his brother John. Jesus gave them the name Sons of Thunder. Sons of Thunder means Children of Thunder.
There was Andrew, and Philip, and Bartholomew, and Matthew, and Thomas, and James the son of Alphaeus. And there was Thaddaeus, and Simon the Zealot.
Judas Iscariot was one of them too. He was the one who was going to betray Jesus to his enemies. Jesus and Beelzebub
Jesus went into a house. The crowd gathered again. It was so large that Jesus and his disciples couldn't even eat.
The family heard about the need. So they went to take care of it. They said "idiot".
There were some teachers of the law there. They had come down from Jerusalem. They said, "He is possessed by Beelzebul! By the prince of demons he is driving out demons."
Jesus called them to himself and said to them in parables, "How can Satan cast out Satan?
If a kingdom wages war against itself, it cannot stand.
If the family splits up, you can't survive.
